WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.669
-The midterm elections
are just months away,

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:06.339
so how concerned should we be
about a foreign power

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.107
once again
meddling in our elections?

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.410
For a look into how vulnerable
our infrastructure is

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.979
to getting hacked,
it's time for "The Check In."

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.947
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.350
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.285
Even before
Trump became president,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.987
he demonstrated
that he didn't really

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.522
take the issue of hacking
too seriously.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.890
How do I know?

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.193
Well, because he publicly
appealed to a foreign adversary

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.395
to continue hacking
into the e-mails

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.797
of his opponent at the time,
Hillary Clinton.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.266
-I will tell you this.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.402
Russia, if you're listening,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:41.608
I hope you're able to find the
30,000 e-mails that are missing.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.310
-That's right -- Trump didn't
just not take it seriously,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.478
he encouraged it.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.113
He's like
one of those parents who say,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.180
"If you kids are gonna drink,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.482
I'd rather you do it
in the house.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.883
And then,
when you're good and buzzed,

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.552
I have shrooms in the freezer.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.021
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:58.224
Now, one of the reasons Russia
was able to hack into the DNC

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.993
and meddle
in our presidential election

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.927
is that we were ill-prepared
for such an attack,

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:03.829
and to be fair,
no one was ready.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:06.232
There was little preparation
and bumbling responses

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.533
from both sides of the aisle.

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:10.202
But now Trump is in charge,
and that's disconcerting,

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:13.473
considering this is how
he talks about cybersecurity

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.107
and technology, in general.

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:17.009
-Now, the cyber is so big.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.278
Maybe there's something
with the crazy computers.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.681
You know, in the old days,
everything was better, right?

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.683
Now you have to open up things,
press a computer.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.151
Takes you 15 minutes.

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:27.787
You know,
we're in a cyber world.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.156
This is now a cyber world.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.525
Russia is knocking us off.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:36.095
We talk about the hacking,
and hacking's bad.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.263
And it shouldn't be done.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.299
A hacker,
some guy with a 200 IQ

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.202
that can't
get up in the morning.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.269
Okay?

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.873
-Sounds like
he's got a handle on it.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.641
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.776
It reminds me of old
"Law &amp; Order" episodes,

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:54.514
where someone tries to explain
the Internet to Lennie Briscoe.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.583
"So you're telling me
I can type something here,

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.718
and somebody else can read it
in another city?

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.086
What a world."

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.121
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:05.225
Okay. So it's clear that Trump
is no expert on this topic,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.959
but at least,
when he became President,

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.896
he had his choice of anyone
he wanted to put in charge

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.731
of cybersecurity,
and he went with a young,

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:15.134
charismatic tech whiz,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.237
even though
he couldn't recognize Rudy

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.171
when he was sitting
right in front of him.

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.474
-I want to introduce
Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.844
And Rudy's very much
of an expert on cybersecurity.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.346
It's been a very important thing
to him and to what he does.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:30.016
And maybe I'll ask Rudy
to say a few words.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.384
Where is Rudy?

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.623 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.328
-He was directly
across the table from him!

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.396
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.264
How was Trump
gonna find the hackers

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:49.902
when he can't even find
Rudy Giuliani at the same table?

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:53.205
No one else
looks like Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.241
Was there another 200-year-old,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.311
bald, beady-eyed man
at the table?

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.746
Now, over a year
after that proclamation,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:00.746
reports say Giuliani's committee

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.448
accomplished
pretty much nothing.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.118
But luckily, Trump didn't just
leave Rudy in charge of it all.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.853
He also tasked Jared Kushner

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.155
with helping
to lead cybersecurity efforts,

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.322
in addition to being in charge

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:12.025
of creating peace
in the Middle East,

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.093
fixing the V.A.,
and solving the opioid crisis

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:17.062
while simultaneously
going through puberty.

00:03:17.062 --> 00:03:19.465
-Many of our federal systems
are decades old.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.868
We are here to improve
the day-to-day lives

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.669
of the average citizen.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:26.038
That's a core promise,
and we are keeping it.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:27.807
-That's right --
Jared Kushner, the guy

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.309
whose previous relationship
to the Internet was --

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.711
I'm guessing --
clearing the search history

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:33.880
before his mom got home?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.115
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.349
"Jared, what are you doing?"

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:40.520
"Oh, just the Middle East!
Fixing the Middle East!"

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.256
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.125
"Just Middle East stuff!"

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.094
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.962
Back in October,
we thought we'd finally

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.465
learn more about what exactly
the administration plans to do

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:55.001
to prevent other countries
from hacking into our databases,

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.037
but, unfortunately, Trump's
cybersecurity czar, Rob Joyce,

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.706
didn't show up to a hearing on
U.S. cyberdefense strategy.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.242
The White House actually
blocked him from testifying,

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.777
citing executive privilege,

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:08.281
resulting in an empty chair with
his name tag during the hearing.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.115
And that only seemed to
encourage Senators

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:12.918
on the committee to
draw attention to his absence.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.988
-The empty chair is outrageous.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.959
We had a foreign government go
at the heart of our democracy.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:25.398
-We see the person in charge
at an empty seat here today.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.600
-But let's be honest --
even when Trump administration

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.535
officials do show up
for questioning,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.437
Senators are also pretty much
just talking to empty chairs.

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:33.806
Just take a look at this.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:37.410
-I-I-I can't answer...
with definitive

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.911
what the conclusion is.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.413
-Yeah, I -- I don't know
what the barriers are.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.749
I don't under--
Senator, I don't understand it.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.016
-Wish I could
give you that number.

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.017
I don't know.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.185
-I-I don't know.
-I don't know.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.120
-I don't know.
-I have no idea.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.488
-Do I know what now?

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.656
-"Know what now?"

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:54.060
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.762
Now this particular empty chair,
Attorney General Jeff Sessions,

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:58.865
announced just last month
that the Department of Justice

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.933
would create
a new cybersecurity task force

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.935
in order
to study election interference.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.104
The DOJ is tasked with providing

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.340
a report on its findings
at the end of June.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.576
But beyond that, we don't know
much more about this task force.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.546
But what we already know
about the situation, in general,

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.880
is that it may be
a little too late

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.615
for more studies and reports.

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.986
-Frankly, the United States
is under attack.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.187
-Russian meddling
is a very real threat

00:05:22.187 --> 00:05:25.291
in the upcoming election,
and the U.S. is unprepared.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.961
-Until we have
some deterrent capacity,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.197
we are going
to continue to be attacked.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.431
-If we don't
change the dynamic here,

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.599
this is gonna continue,
and 2016 won't be viewed

00:05:34.599 --> 00:05:36.101
as something isolated.

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:39.238
This is something that
will be sustained over time.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.573
-Now, if that's
not enough to scare you,

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.809
that guy right there,
NSA chief Mike Rogers,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.677
who's actually
retiring this Spring,

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.446
also indicated that he hasn't
received orders from Trump

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:50.083
to disrupt Russian cyberattacks
targeting elections.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.784
And after months
and months of inaction,

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:55.420
the State Department
was finally given $120 million

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.089
to fight
Russian election meddling.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:06:01.894
And of that $120 million,
it has spent zero dollars.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.228
Now, to be fair,
the Trump administration

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:04.763
is probably
saving all that money

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:07.533
for goodbye cakes for all the
people leaving the White House.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.569
That's not official.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:13.272
It's just, we're taping at 6:30,
so it's a guess.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.208
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.977
Meanwhile, the Senate
is still waiting.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:21.513
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:24.149
Still waiting to get detailed
cybersecurity plans

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:25.418
from this administration.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.386
Because right now,
Trump's cyber plan

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:28.687
seems to boil down to...

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:30.055
-Do I know what now?

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:32.024
-This has been "The Check In."

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.792
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.395
[ Bell dings ]

